      <h2 id="evidence">Is there a best time to take collagen?</h2>

      <p>
        Not one that has been tested. We searched for trials comparing morning with evening, or fasted
        with fed, for collagen's effect on skin, joints or bone, and found none. The confident answers
        online are reasonable guesses, usually from sellers, presented as findings.
      </p>

      <p>
        What the positive trials did control was consistency: the same full dose, every day, for 8 to 24
        weeks. That is the variable with evidence behind it. Our article on
        <a href="/pages/how-long-does-collagen-take-to-work">how long collagen takes to work</a> explains
        why missing days matters more than the hour you take it, and
        <a href="/pages/how-much-collagen-per-day">how much collagen per day</a> covers the doses those
        trials used.
      </p>

